A||N||6||Iron Duke Wellingsley||How?removing the left and right parking brake cables||||5||
Z||000000||Iron Duke Wellingsley||05-28-2001||01:15 AM||||I am replacing the emergency brake cables on my 84 sport coupe.<P>The cables are held in the cradle with three-prong "tangs" that prevent them from being pulled out.  There are some openings in the cradle, so I could push the tangs in on one side, but then there's still two others holding the cable in there.  If I try to yank the cable out, then the tangs will get bent out and lock the cable in place.<P>Do you cut them in some way?  Or, is there some big-$ tool that I need.  <P>Please, tell me how easy this is and HOW you do it.<P>Thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||tgowens||05-28-2001||02:32 AM||||I just pull out and to one side with one hand while snapping the prongs through with the blade of a screwdriver..........takes a little getting used to.....||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||05-28-2001||07:37 AM||||I use a pair of pliers to squeeze the tabs in...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000003||87GTjoe||05-28-2001||08:58 AM||||I pulled it in the center and then put vise grips on each end to keep the slack in the cable.Real easy.||||reg||1
Z||000004||87GTjoe||05-28-2001||09:00 AM||||sorry,mine is a 87 I guess its different.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ken Wittlief||05-28-2001||10:43 AM||||If you look at the new ones you'll see that clip can be pried off sideways too, its like a big snap ring on the end of the cable.||||reg||1
Z||000006||kslish||05-28-2001||03:04 PM||||I just did this before Carlisle (winter weather isn't kind to these cables).  It's hard to describe, but once you do one to get the hang of it, the other side will be a LOT easier.  <P>What I did was push in the prongs one at a time with a flat blade screwdriver while pulling on the cable housing and then rotating it some to get to expose the next prong through the slot in the cradle.  You have to constantly be pulling on the cable some because if you release it the prongs will snap back out.  It would probably be easier as a 2 person operation (one to push in the prongs with the screwdriver while another pulls on the cable), but I was able to do it by myself.<P>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> ||||reg||1
